</script>
</figure>

I say that {A|At} is also similar to {B|Bt}.

Since {A|At} is similar to {C|Ct}, it is equiangular with it and has the sides about the equal angles proportional. [!just VI.Def.1]

Again, since {B|Bt} is similar to {C|Ct}, it is equiangular with it and has the sides about the equal angles proportional.

Therefore each of the figures {A|At} and {B|Bt} is equiangular with {C|Ct} and with {C|Ct} has the sides about the equal angles proportional, therefore {A|At} is similar to {B|Bt}. [!just V.11]

Therefore, *figures which are similar to the same rectilinear figure are also similar to one another.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
